Adrian

Thanks for reporting your problem.  The University email system would not accept your attachment, but I could access it from the Google groups site.

The situation is just as you report it; coordinates of your shape file and coordinates of your coverage grid locations carry opposite signs.  Not very useful for computing evenness of competing survey designs.

Two (possibly random) ideas:

I see the shapefile name inside the Bagual_PM.dat subdirectory is not "Study_ar.shp", but rather "Costa_PM.shp".  I was of the belief that shape files needed to have that specific name; perhaps my understanding is outdated.

Is there any chance the coordinates of the shape file could have been in the "wrong" order; clockwise rather than counter-clockwise (or whichever direction is expected of shape files)?

